    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 3.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif ðonne se frigea ðy dæge wyrce butan his hlafordes hæse, ðolie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.9"/> his freotes.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.11"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>. . . ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> se frigea þy dæge wyrce buton hlafordes hæse, þolie his freotes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> se frigea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/> ðy dæge wyrce buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.2"/> his hlafordes hæse, ðolige his freotes (oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.7"/> LX scll'; ⁊ preost twyscildig).</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf ðonne se frigea ðy dæge wyrce buton his hlafordes hǽse, ðolie his freotes oððe sixtig scill'; ⁊ preost<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.1"/> twyscyldi.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Si liber ea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.6"/> die operetur sine iussu domini sui, perdat libertatem suam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="36" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif ðonne se frigea ðy dæge wyrce butan his hlafordes hæse, ðolie his freotes [oððe LX scll'; ⁊ preost twyscildig<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_3-2.attnote.fn.10"/>].</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="372" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif þonne se frigea ðy dæge wyrce butan his hlafordes hæse, þolie his freotes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn aber der Freie an jenem Tage arbeitet ohne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.de.1"/> seines Herrn Geheiss, verliere er seine Freiheit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.de.2"/> (oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.de.3"/> 60 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.de.4"/>; und ein Priester<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_3-2.lnote.de.5"/> [sei] doppelt schuldig).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if the freeman works on that day without his lord’s command, let him lose his freedom (or 60 shillings; and a priest [is to be] doubly liable).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="37" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, a freeman works on that day, except by his lord's command, he shall be reduced to slavery, or [pay a fine of] 60 shillings. A priest shall pay a double fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="400" ed="#whitelock"/>If then a freeman works on that day without his lord’s command, he is to forfeit his freedom.<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_3-2.whinote.n.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="373" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If, however, a freeman works on that day without his lord’s command, let him pay with his freedom.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="469"><ref target="clause:IICn_45-1">II Cn 45.1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. zugefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si added in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> oper. ipsa die <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; oper. ipsa die the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ge <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ge written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oððe <hi rend="italic">bis</hi> twysc. <hi rend="italic">am Rande,</hi> 12. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oððe to twysc. in the margin, 12th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þolige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þolige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oþþe sixtig scillinges, ⁊ preost sy twyscildig <hi rend="italic">fügt Ld zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oþþe sixtig scillinges, ⁊ preost sy twyscildig added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gefolge 20</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gefolge 20</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Verknechtung 7b. 10. 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Verknechtung 7b. 10. 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wie Ine 3, 1³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">As Ine 3, 1³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu erklären entweder als Preis des Unfreien (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7a) oder aus höherem Strafgeld in 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">To be explained either as the price of an unfree man (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7a) or from the higher fine in 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_3-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Doppelstrafe für Geistliche (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 27b) findet in der Doppelstrafe für den seine Amtseingesessenen beraubenden Vogt (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 11d) Parallele: der Amtscharakter verlangt Sonntagsfeier (bzw. Eigentumschutz) vom Priester (bzw. Richter) besonders. — Offenbar ist an bäuerlich arbeitende Landpfarrer gedacht. — Empfänger des Strafgelds scheint auch hier wie in 2. 4 der König. Hinzuzudenken ist kirchliche Pönitenz</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The double penalty for clergy (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 27b) has a parallel in the double penalty for the reeve who robs the inhabitants of his district (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 11d): the character of the office requires of the priest Sunday observance, and of the judge protection of property, in particular. — Evidently country priests who do farm work are meant. — Here too, as in 2. 4, the recipient of the fine appears to be the king. Ecclesiastical penance is to be understood in addition</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_3-2.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">36</biblScope></bibl><label>twyscildig</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">B, H*.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 10 is printed 2 times on the page (3.1, 3.2), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_3-2.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">400</biblScope></bibl><label>freedom</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">ibid, adds: “or 60 shillings, and a priest is doubly liable”</seg></note>
      </div>
